{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Clock","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:12_Concurrency5ClockP8DurationQa","text":"Duration","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Clock\/Duration"},{"text":"> : ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:s8SendableP","text":"Sendable","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Sendable"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["macOS"]}]},{"content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Types that conform to the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Clock"},{"type":"text","text":" protocol define a concept of “now” which"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is the specific instant in time that property is accessed. Any pair of calls"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"now"},{"type":"text","text":" property may have a minimum duration between them - this"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"minimum resolution is exposed by the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"minimumResolution"},{"type":"text","text":" property to inform"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"any user of the type the expected granularity of accuracy."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"One of the primary uses for clocks is to schedule task sleeping. This method"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"resumes the calling task after a given deadline has been met or passed with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a given tolerance value. The tolerance is expected as a leeway around the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"deadline. The clock may reschedule tasks within the tolerance to ensure"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"efficient execution of resumptions by reducing potential operating system"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"wake-ups. If no tolerance is specified (i.e. nil is passed in) the sleep"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"function is expected to schedule with a default tolerance strategy."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For more information about specific clocks see "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ContinuousClock"},{"type":"text","text":" and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SuspendingClock"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"topicSections":[{"generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Clock\/Duration","doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Clock\/Instant"],"title":"Associated Types","anchor":"Associated-Types"},{"title":"Instance Properties","generated":true,"anchor":"Instance-Properties","identifiers":["doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Clock\/minimumResolution","doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Clock\/now"]},{"title":"Instance Methods","generated":true,"anchor":"Instance-Methods","identifiers":["doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Clock\/enqueue(_:on:at:tolerance:)","doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Clock\/measure(_:)","doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Clock\/measure(isolation:_:)","doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Clock\/run(_:at:tolerance:)","doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Clock\/sleep(for:tolerance:)","doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Clock\/sleep(until:tolerance:)"]},{"title":"Type Properties","generated":true,"anchor":"Type-Properties","identifiers":["doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Clock\/continuous","doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Clock\/suspending"]}],"relationshipsSections":[{"type":"inheritsFrom","title":"Inherits From",